  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Texas Army Trail is the long, open test at Cypress's Bud Hadfield Park — 18 holes at par 58 across 6,688 feet, with long distance holes that demand accuracy more than raw power. Chuck Haney's 2011 design has alternate pins on eight holes to keep it fresh.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and Mach 7 baskets, and very cart friendly. The open fairways make every drive visible and every mistake obvious — a great course for learning to throw long and straight.",
    "A friendly-but-serious round that's become a Houston-area favorite."
  ],
